15
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:33,000
I had a similar problem with blue cards when a council summer camp

16
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:38,000
issued completed merit badges on a computer printout versus the blue card.

17
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:41,000
I simply had scouts put their information on blue cards,

18
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:46,000
stapled a copy of the forms the camp gave us to the blue card for our records,

19
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:51,000
supplied the scout with their portion of the blue card with another copy of the form on it.

20
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:55,000
It was a pretty quick, easy solution to the problem

21
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:00,000
And we know that the official blue card. that application for a merit badge

22
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:02,000
is supposed to be the only accepted form.

23
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:04,000
Some people get it wrong once in a while.

24
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:06,000
We don't make the scouts suffer,

25
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:08,000
We try and find a way to solve it.

26
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Francine, it sounds like you found a way.

27
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:12,000
Thank you very much for letting us know.

28
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:16,000
Alan Schneider is the scout master of troop 483..

29
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:21,000
He said I enjoyed your segment on patrols planning menus that one scout doesn't like.

30
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:24,000
I've had new scouts come into the troop

31
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:27,000
and it seems like their parents allow them to be picky eaters

32
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:30,000
and they prepare their own meals for them and things like that,

33
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:35,000
which is really almost impossible for a patrol to deal with.

34
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:38,000
But if they work at it they find a way.

35
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:42,000
If a patrol works with a scout who's got a problem with the menu,

36
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:45,000
they learn to adjust their habits as a patrol

37
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:47,000
and the scout himself learns something.

38
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:51,000
Actually, by the end of the first year in scouts, one mom came to me

39
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:55,000
and said she couldn't believe her son was now eating so many different meals

40
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:58,000
that she'd never been able to get him to eat before.

41
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Well, you know what,

42
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:02,000
When you don't have a whole lot of choices,

43
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:05,000
sometimes you adjust your menu a little bit.

44
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:07,000
You adjust what's acceptable to eat,

45
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:10,000
and a patrol can work around that,

46
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:13,000
And it's surprising what kind of solutions they come up with

47
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:16,000
when we put the problem in their hands.

48
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:18,000
They'll need a little advice

49
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:20,000
and things usually end up working out, don't they?

50
